# Human / Secret Boundary

This stage intentionally separates the local Codex coordinator from credential custody.

## Human-only / never expose to Codex

- independent admin private SSH key;
- owner signing private key;
- cloud account password/token/recovery codes;
- API keys or service-account private material;
- any secret that can mint/recover root authority.

Do not paste these values into chat, files in the Codex workspace, shell history visible to Codex, or the return packet.

## Safe public inputs Codex may receive

- admin SSH public key and public-key fingerprint;
- VPS host public fingerprint;
- public package hashes;
- receipt paths/IDs and their public hashes;
- old/new boot identity;
- explicit human classification of the root RSA fingerprint based on real provenance;
- PASS/FAIL of provider-console recovery proof and cloud-regrant neutralization, plus non-secret evidence locator.

## Recommended interaction pattern

The human establishes/authenticates the independent channel outside the Codex-readable workspace (for example through provider console/recovery or a human-controlled credential agent). Codex may coordinate commands and verify public outputs, but must not open/read the private credential.

If this separation cannot be maintained, stop with `WAITING_FOR_INDEPENDENT_ADMIN_ACTION`.

# P5 Failure, Resume and Session-Recovery Protocol V3

The conversation is not state. Receipts + live VPS + Research Memory are state.

On any session loss:
1. start a fresh conversation; never `--continue`/`--resume` an untrusted old P5 transcript;
2. re-run T-1 bundle/context gate;
3. re-establish k3 transport through T0 if needed;
4. read `STATE/P5_ACTIVATION_STATE_V3.json` only as a hint;
5. independently verify receipts/live state;
6. identify the first transition that is not mechanically proven;
7. resume exactly there.

Never rerun a committed mutation simply because the chat forgot it. Never advance because a prior chat claimed PASS without receipt/live proof.

Failure classes:
- hash/release mismatch -> HASH_MISMATCH_STOP;
- instruction-surface conflict -> INSTRUCTION_SURFACE_CONFLICT_STOP;
- unexpected runtime state -> STATE_DRIFT_STOP;
- independent-admin unavailable -> WAITING_FOR_INDEPENDENT_ADMIN_ACTION;
- owner TCB signature missing -> WAITING_FOR_OWNER_TCB_SIGNATURE;
- owner root late-bound input missing -> WAITING_FOR_OWNER_ROOT_LATE_BOUND_INPUTS;
- owner root signature missing -> WAITING_FOR_OWNER_ROOT_SIGNATURE;
- exact ceremony gate failure -> CEREMONY_GATE_FAILED_EXACTLY;
- T1 TEST_VOIDED -> T1_TEST_VOIDED_STOP;
- W1 resource expiry -> same logical wave checkpoint/resume only.

After the first real P3 label-access marker, do not patch science/runtime and pretend the rerun is a clean first look. Any integrity defect follows the frozen TEST_VOIDED/failure governance; no ad-hoc rerun or label-dependent repair.

No broad Linux, F01-F08, PC6 methodology or alpha-idea review is triggered by a narrow operational failure.
